A||||5||Ironhorse||Interior trims and etc||||6||
Z||000000||Ironhorse||04-21-2000||01:23 PM||||I yanked out EVERYTHING in the interior except for the main dash of my new/old 85 fiero GT... I found 15 year old of dust, ciggs ashes, and etc... makes me madder than hell that anyone would treat this car so terribly.  I bought some Brown Bomber 52 cleaner (STRONGEST SH*T I'VE EVER USED) It has akalaka acid in it is why it's strong. It cleaned out EVERYTHING that's stuck on the trim panel, dash, insterment panel dash, center console.  Here a thing... It does not take out the sun faded look  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> I'll need to repaint the trim and etc..  Can anyone tell me the most effective way to repaint vynal, and plastic?  I can't afford to take it to professional and I'm not gonna replace them for a new one cuz they are all in PUUUURRRRFECT condition. I also would like to know the name of product to clean them.. The good stuff not those 99 cent a can stuff from Odd Lot  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Thanks||||reg||6
Z||000001||Raydar||04-21-2000||01:40 PM||||Strangely enough, the best cleaner I've ever used was called "Mean Green". Think it came from Big Lots. Unfortunately, I can't find any more. (If you find some, make sure it's safe for plastic and vinyl. I think it is.)<BR>Simple Green is similar, but didn't seem to work as well, and smells worse.<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-21-2000||02:06 PM||||I found Simple Green works best diluted 10:1 or more. I like the citrus cleaners for allot of things. They small nice and will eat off nearly any kind of dirt. The citrus hand cleaners are the only ones I use now. ((Except emergencies when I use some GOOP in the toothpaste tube package. You can carry that one around and not have to worry about it leaking in the car.))||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ironhorse||04-21-2000||04:02 PM||||This brown stealth was soemthing I came across my local part shop... I had to dilute it like 14 to 1 and it works great!  Now how bout some answer to my question about type of paint and method of painting viyal and plastic trims  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||TheFiero64||04-21-2000||06:08 PM||||I like to use Castrol Super Clean. I use it on everything including using it as a degreaser. It has cleaned everything I have used it on. After I use Formula 2001 Protectant to get rid of any sun faded or dull areas. It works 10 times better than Armor All. It also has a nice leather smell.<P><p>[This message has been edited by TheFiero64 (edited 04-21-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||04-22-2000||05:34 AM||||I dyed the large rear panels in my Mustang (were gray now black) I went to my local auto parts store and got a can of Dupli-color interior dye. It was about $5.00 a can.I cleaned the panels and made sure they were dry. I sprayed about 10 very light coats (over 2 days) on them and let the final coat dry for 2 more days. They came out 100% perfect. You cant even scratch it off ..After you install them back into your car use Armor All dash protectant in the black bottle (It wont attract dust and dirt)I hope this helps...let me know. Good Luck||||reg||10
